# Wardrobe v0.1.0

Wardrobe is an offline-first Android wardrobe app paired with a local Python
generation pipeline. This first portfolio release includes a synthetic demo
wardrobe, so the app can be explored without personal photos, API keys, model
downloads, or a running backend.

## Highlights

- Capture and export pose and clothing inputs on Android.
- Browse generated outfits, filters, favorites, edits, and regeneration state.
- Classify locally with Qwen3-VL through Ollama and render with FLUX.2 [klein]
  4B through ComfyUI.
- Create headwear and shoe cutouts with GroundingDINO and Segment Anything.
- Reproduce the complete file pipeline with the deterministic mock smoke test.

## Android download

`wardrobe-v0.1.0-android-universal.apk` is a signed universal APK for ARM64,
ARMv7, and x86_64 Android devices. Size: **{{APK_SIZE}}**.

This app is distributed directly through GitHub rather than Google Play.
Android will ask you to allow installation from your browser or file manager.
Only install the asset downloaded from this release.

- APK SHA-256: `{{APK_SHA256}}`
- Signing-certificate SHA-256: `{{CERTIFICATE_SHA256}}`

The APK requests no normal Internet, camera, or broad external-storage
permission. The bundled synthetic content works offline.

## Verification

- 74 Python tests, Ruff, and deterministic ZIP smoke test.
- 91 Flutter tests, format check, static analysis, and Android builds.
- Real local Ollama → ComfyUI → GroundingDINO/SAM → pack → Android import run.
- Visual Android checks for the generated base outfit, beanie, and shoe overlays.
- Privacy audit of the release tree, Git history, archive contents, and images.

See `docs/VERIFICATION.md` for the exercised paths and `README.md` for setup.

## Known limitations

- Android is the only end-to-end supported app target.
- The full AI pipeline requires substantial local model setup and storage.
- Generated image quality can vary and may require rerendering or review.
- The APK is sideloaded from GitHub and is not distributed through Google Play.
